# Cinders of Chaos encrypted client pack (client/BASE.md "Client packs"). The client ships one file beside the exe,
# chaos.pack: a deterministic store-only ZIP of the whole client tree (init.lua, data/, modules/, mods/, layouts/),
# compressed as one zlib stream (level 9) and encrypted as one blob with AES-256-GCM (OpenSSL and zlib, which the client
# links already). Pack format version 2: compressing before encrypting keeps the download near the size of a plain zip.
# The engine streams the pack from disk, decrypting and inflating each 4 MB chunk straight into one buffer of the ZIP's
# size (no ciphertext buffer, no second copy), and mounts it through the existing PhysFS memory-archive path, so every
# module keeps reading files through g_resources unchanged and the shipped folder is just the exe and this one file.
#   * src/framework/util/chaospack.h (new, header only; vectors in client/tools/chaospack_test.cpp): AES-256-GCM,
#     HKDF-SHA256 key derivation and the zlib layer, byte-identical to the packing tool client/tools/pack_client.py.
#     The pack header (magic, version 2, flags, 12-byte nonce, uncompressed ZIP length) is the GCM AAD, so any tamper
#     fails. decryptStream() keeps the output only when the tag verifies and inflate ends exactly at the declared size.
#   * src/framework/core/resourcemanager.{h,cpp}: mountEncryptedPack(key) finds chaos.pack beside the exe, streams it
#     through decryptStream() with the key and mounts the result from memory (mountMemoryData); setup() and
#     getCompactName() use the mounted pack. A wrong key or a corrupt pack is fatal; no pack present (a dev tree of
#     loose files) returns false and loads as before.
#   * src/main.cpp: before init.lua is read, derive the pack key from the client guard key (chaosguard::builtInKey(),
#     base patch 0035 - no new secret) and mount the pack, then wipe the key. The app name is "CindersOfChaos", so the
#     per-user write dir (config.otml, logs, the updater tree) is named after it, never next to the exe.
#   * init.lua: APP_NAME "CindersOfChaos" (the compact name, config dir and <name>.log file).
# This deters copying; it does not stop a determined reverse engineer, since the key is in the binary (obfuscated the
# way chaosguard_key.h is). Apply after 0001-0101: tools/assemble_client.sh applies every patch in order.
